  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book by Lorena Velázquez M.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Comprises 22 stiff black boards bound in accordion fold format; printed on both sides in white, silver, and red with mounted photographs. The boards are 21.5 x 21.5 cm each, except for the first board, which is 21.5 x 11 cm and has red cord laced along the unbound edge.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Cuarenta y tres ejemplares numerados y firm a dos por la autora de 1/43 a 43/43 ... Con la participación: Autora, Lorena Velázquez. Composición tipográfica, Luis Rodríguez y Makeba Gil. Fotografías, Vicente Guijosa y Lorena Velázquez. Encuadernación, Francisco Lara Mazaba, asistente Adriana Chávez. Impresión de imágenes, Gabriel Figueroa. Impresión en serigrafía, Jorge Jiménez Colio. Texto, Anónimus."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Commentary on the murder of 43 Mexican students in Iguala in the Mexican state of Guerrero on September 26, 2014, from Ayontzinapa Rural Teachers' College, and the protests that followed regarding the criminal investigation into, and those responisible for, their deaths.</subfield>
  </datafield>
